      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: recover MCP OAuth sessions after token refresh",
        "body": "Closes #98377.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\nLong-running gateway MCP sessions could stay stuck after OAuth access-token expiry when the refreshed bearer was rejected on the old streamable HTTP MCP session.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nThe session MCP runtime now treats OAuth streamable HTTP 401s as stale-session failures, retires the current MCP transport once, rebuilds the catalog/session, and replays the request through the existing refresh-token path. Static-header and non-OAuth MCP failures keep the existing failure/backoff behavior.\n\n## User Impact\nHeadless gateways can recover OAuth-protected remote MCP servers without requiring a manual `openclaw mcp login` while a valid refresh token exists.\n\n## Evidence\nAdded deterministic streamable HTTP OAuth regressions for catalog refresh, direct tool calls, and failed retry/backoff preservation.\n\nReal gateway proof with `startGatewayServer`, the QA mock provider, and a local streamable-http OAuth MCP server. The server expired the access token immediately after gateway cataloging, then rejected the refreshed bearer on the stale MCP session:\n\n```text\ngateway proof result: OpenClaw gateway response completed after OAuth expiry\ngateway proof final: MCP_CODE_MODE_FILE_OK note=fixture-note-alpha unclear=none improvement=virtual-api-files-were-clear-and-needed-one-exec\ngateway proof counts: token_refreshes=1 initialize_calls=2\nredacted OAuth/MCP server transcript:\n- initialize session=- token=initial-access -> 200 stale-session\n- notifications/initialized session=stale-session token=initial-access -> 202\n- tools/list session=stale-session token=initial-access -> 200\n- server/expire session=stale-session token=initial-access -> access token expired after catalog\n- tools/call session=stale-session token=initial-access -> 401 invalid_token\n- POST /token session=- token=refresh-token -> 200 refreshed-access\n- tools/call session=stale-session token=refreshed-access -> 401 stale_mcp_session\n- initialize session=- token=refreshed-access -> 200 fresh-session\n- notifications/initialized session=fresh-session token=refreshed-access -> 202\n- tools/list session=fresh-session token=refreshed-access -> 200\n- tools/call session=fresh-session token=refreshed-access -> 200 fixture-note-alpha:fresh-session\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix-98377-mcp-oauth-gateway-refresh",
        "head_sha": "2e8b2e6a8fdecdb3e9647def067f1bedbb3bf225",
